 * in the row, so it can return 12.5, -20 or 200; this value flows straight into
 * `vpsTermPriceCents` and from there into a wallet debit, a Stripe amount and an
 * Invoice line. A rate over 100 would price the annual term NEGATIVE (paying the
 * customer to buy), and a negative one would inflate it past 12× monthly — the same
 * class of silent money bug the other add-on readers clamp against. The admin panel
 * refuses out-of-range on write (lib/actions-settings.ts); this clamp defends the
 * charge paths against a hand-written row that slipped past it.
 */
